From: PowOS <powos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] xwayland: KGSL paces async flips on the frame callback

0014's line named KWin's "2 commits per drawn frame": there is no second commit - every one is a flip (2500 flip
commits / 30 s, all damaged, 0 others) while KWin's window task draws ~40/s and frame callbacks come back ~29/s.
Broforce (DXVK on Wine's X11 Vulkan WSI) presents with PresentOptionAsync (immediate/mailbox), and upstream completes
an async flip on a wl_display_sync round trip, so each of its ~84 presents/s went to KWin as a commit (a transaction,
a dma-buf fence wait) and KWin dropped half of them. On KGSL an async flip now waits for the frame callback like a
vsync'd one; upstream's flip-queue mailbox replaces an older queued flip with the newest (it completes as skipped and
its buffer goes back to the client idle), so one drawn frame = one commit and the shown frame is still the newest.
Counted on 0014's line: "async flips paced N, skipped N".
---
diff --git a/hw/xwayland/xwayland-present.c b/hw/xwayland/xwayland-present.c
index b72cc1e..d75ab01 100644
--- a/hw/xwayland/xwayland-present.c
+++ b/hw/xwayland/xwayland-present.c
@@ -1155,6 +1155,19 @@ retry:
         return;
     }
 
+#ifdef XWL_HAS_GLAMOR
+    /* PowOS 0015: on KGSL an async flip waits for the compositor's frame callback like a vsync'd one (mailbox: the
+     * newest queued flip replaces an older one below, which completes as skipped and goes back to the client idle).
+     * Upstream completes an async flip on a wl_display_sync round trip, so a game in immediate/mailbox mode
+     * (Broforce: DXVK on Wine's X11 WSI, ~84 presents/s) committed every frame while KWin's window task draws
+     * ~40/s: 2500 flip commits / 30 s for ~1200 drawn, each one a KWin transaction and fence wait for a frame it then
+     * dropped (kwin 3.65 probe + 0014's line, 2026-11-05). */
+    if (vblank->flip && !vblank->sync_flip && !notify_only && xwl_glamor_is_kgsl_surfaceless(xwl_screen)) {
+        vblank->sync_flip = TRUE;
+        xwl_kgsl_commits.paced++;
+    }
+#endif /* XWL_HAS_GLAMOR */
+
     if (flip_pending && vblank->flip && !notify_only) {
         present_vblank_ptr flip_queued_last;
 
@@ -1171,6 +1184,7 @@ retry:
 #endif
              )) {
             xorg_list_del(&flip_queued_last->event_queue);
+            xwl_kgsl_commits.skipped++;  /* PowOS 0015: a frame the compositor would have dropped */
             present_vblank_scrap(flip_queued_last);
             xwl_present_re_execute(flip_queued_last);
         }
